[l_english.STATE_LORE_46]
Beneath the glass dome of the Weather Lab, colorful failures drift endlessly. The scientist ponies still firmly believe that with just one more experiment, they could end Equestria’s eternal winter with a rainbow generator — though the last time they said that, they blew half the roof off the lab.
This was once a place where the line between genius and madness blurred beyond recognition. The archives are stuffed with absurd proposals like “harnessing hurricanes for power”, “turning clouds into cotton candy to rain chocolate” and “creating rainbows by moving really fast”. Yet buried among them are a few era-defining breakthroughs — ironically, many of those forementioned mad ideas somehow became reality in the strangest ways.
The cruelest twist came when, amid the cold and darkness, the lab finally found a solution hidden within thousands of utterly useless patents — only to realize that the Weather Factory, the very place that could have brought their ideas to life, had long since fallen silent under snow and rebellion.
Now, tour guides love showing off the rusted experimental devices to visitors. As for those white-coated visionaries? Some still linger in the Meteorological Bureau with cushy sinecures, sipping tea and reading newspapers. Others peddle spin-off products like cotton candy or syrup-drenched ice cream. And then there are those who became the least popular drunks in taverns — always muttering something about “if only we’d gotten three more months of funding”...

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_46]
天气实验室的玻璃穹顶下永远漂浮着五彩斑斓的失败品。那些科研小马们至今仍坚信，只要再给他们一次实验机会，就能用彩虹发生器终结小马利亚的寒冬 —— 虽然他们上次这么说时，炸飞了半个实验室的屋顶。
这里曾是天才与疯子的分界线模糊不清的地方，档案室里堆满了诸如“用飓风发电”、“把云层改造成棉花糖下巧克力雨”、“通过高速移动制造彩虹”的荒谬提案，偶尔也会翻出几份改变时代的杰作：比如前文那些疯子们的提案后来似乎都以奇怪的方式实现了。
讽刺的是，面对寒冷与黑暗，当实验室终于在数以万计完全无用的专利申请中发现了解决思路的时候，帮助他们将这些想法付诸实践的天气工厂，早已在风雪与起义中停止了运转。
如今导游们喜欢向游客展示那些生锈的实验装置。而当年那些穿着白大褂的狂想家们，有的还在气象局挂着闲职喝茶看报，有的开始兜售棉花糖或者糖浆冰激凌等衍生产品，有的则成了酒馆里最不受欢迎的醉汉 —— 他们总在嘟囔着什么“如果当年经费再多批三个月”...
